+````markdown name=ops/hsm/hsm_activation_checklist_aws.md
+```text
+AWS CloudHSM + KMS Custom Key Store Activation Checklist (Operator)
+
+Preconditions:
+ - Terraform resources for CloudHSM cluster created and you have the cluster id (see ops/hsm/aws_cloudhsm_full.tf).
+ - Operator AWS CLI configured with an account that can create & initialize CloudHSM and KMS custom key stores.
+ - Vault reachable & operator has vault CLI permissions to write keys.
+ - EVIDENCE_BUCKET (s3) configured for audit artifacts.
+
+Step 0 — Prepare
+ - Pick custodians: Key Admin, Key Officer, Auditor.
+ - Create an operator-runner host with aws cli, cosign, jq, and vault cli.
+
+Step 1 — Initialize CloudHSM
+ - Run: aws cloudhsmv2 describe-clusters --cluster-id <cluster-id> --region <region>
+ - Follow AWS guide to initialize cluster: create the cluster certificates and run:
+     aws cloudhsmv2 initialize-cluster --cluster-id <cluster-id> --signed-cert file://clusterCert.pem
+ - Confirm all HSMs show status ACTIVE in describe-clusters.
+
+Step 2 — Create KMS Custom Key Store
+ - In the KMS console, create a "Custom key store" and point it to the CloudHSM cluster.
+ - Wait for custom key store to reach "CONNECTED" state.
+
+Step 3 — Create asymmetric signing key (CMK)
+ - Create a CMK in KMS using the custom key store:
+     aws kms create-key --customer-master-key-spec RSA_3072 --key-usage SIGN_VERIFY --origin AWS_CLOUDHSM
+ - Record the key ARN.
+
+Step 4 — Record issuance manifest & Vault staging
+ - Run:
+     python3 ops/hsm/issue_key_manifest.py --key-ref <key-arn> --operator "Alice" --notes "Initial issuance"
+ - Upload manifest to EVIDENCE_BUCKET (issue_key_manifest.py will do this if EVIDENCE_BUCKET configured).
+ - Put the new key ref into Vault staging path:
+     vault kv put secret/data/aegis/kms/staging cosign_key_refs="<aws-kms://<key-arn>>"
+
+Step 5 — Auditor review & cosign
+ - Auditor reviews manifest and cosigns if required (manual).
+ - After audit OK, promote staging to active:
+     vault kv put secret/data/aegis/kms cosign_key_refs="<aws-kms://<key-arn>>"
+
+Step 6 — Smoke test cosign
+ - Create a sample artifact:
+     echo "aegis-test" > /tmp/aegis_test.tar.gz
+ - Sign:
+     cosign sign --key aws-kms://<key-arn> /tmp/aegis_test.tar.gz
+ - Verify:
+     cosign verify --key aws-kms://<key-arn> /tmp/aegis_test.tar.gz
+
+Step 7 — Rotation drill
+ - Follow ops/hsm/rotation_ceremony.md and ops/hsm/rotate_keys_prod.sh to add a new key in staging, get approvals, re-sign artifacts, verify, and retire old key.
+
+Step 8 — Operationalize
+ - Create documented custody roster in your Vault or SSO group.
+ - Schedule quarterly rotation and record all rotation events via ops/hsm/audit_rotation_log.py.
+ - Integrate delegation_enforcer.py into orchestrators to require M‑of‑N approvals for sensitive actions.
+
+Security notes:
+ - Limit signer principals in KMS key policy to narrowly scoped roles.
+ - Maintain offline/backed-up paper trail of manifests and keep an audit read-only copy in evidence bucket.
+ - Test emergency kill-switch: ops/hsm/kill_switch.sh disable
+
+````
